00:27:16.170 --> 00:27:17.670
What are you doing in LA by the way?

590
00:27:17.670 --> 00:27:20.001
I'm gonna Coachella and I had meetings.

591
00:27:20.001 --> 00:27:22.590
So I had some night meetings in LA business stuff

592
00:27:22.590 --> 00:27:23.850
and then Coachella,

593
00:27:23.850 --> 00:27:25.350
mom and dad are gonna

594
00:27:25.350 --> 00:27:26.940
out on these streets.
First trip away

595
00:27:26.940 --> 00:27:28.380
that you're doing.

596
00:27:28.380 --> 00:27:32.040
It's great, I love being a mom.

597
00:27:32.040 --> 00:27:33.690
Athena is a cool human,

598
00:27:33.690 --> 00:27:37.110
like she's just exudes a level of cool

599
00:27:37.110 --> 00:27:41.360
that is really humbling.

600
00:27:41.360 --> 00:27:45.720
I mean, she's just a cool human, I love being her mom.

601
00:27:45.720 --> 00:27:47.820
It's felt very intuitive to be honest.

602
00:27:47.820 --> 00:27:49.293
I wanna say that it's been,

603
00:27:52.740 --> 00:27:54.810
I mean, honestly, it's been kind of easy.

604
00:27:54.810 --> 00:27:58.102
Like I guess, I shouldn't say easy, simple, straightforward.

605
00:27:58.102 --> 00:27:59.236
Like it's like,

606
00:27:59.236 --> 00:28:01.968
that's my kid and that's my husband and that's my family

607
00:28:01.968 --> 00:28:03.488
and it feels good.

608
00:28:03.488 --> 00:28:04.950
And how do you think about like,

609
00:28:04.950 --> 00:28:08.880
have you developed an evolving philosophy of motherhood

610
00:28:08.880 --> 00:28:12.573
and on that subject of balance or anti balance,

611
00:28:13.410 --> 00:28:17.310
how do you think about continuing to pursue your dreams

612
00:28:17.310 --> 00:28:19.890
and your goals while also being the mother

613
00:28:19.890 --> 00:28:23.070
that you want to be and making all of that work?

614
00:28:23.070 --> 00:28:27.510
I am more ambitious now as a mom, I think.

615
00:28:27.510 --> 00:28:29.793
And I was pretty ambitious before Athena.

616
00:28:31.822 --> 00:28:33.180
I mean, it goes back to some of the things

617
00:28:33.180 --> 00:28:34.013
we already talked about.

618
00:28:34.013 --> 00:28:37.740
Like, I am unapologetic with my no

619
00:28:37.740 --> 00:28:42.740
and I have boundaries that like I will not do meetings,

620
00:28:43.830 --> 00:28:46.230
executive meetings or otherwise with my agents

621
00:28:46.230 --> 00:28:49.203
after five o'clock like, I won't, I put my phone,

622
00:28:49.203 --> 00:28:51.750
like I don't have notifications on my phone.

623
00:28:51.750 --> 00:28:55.863
I don't, like the thing I use as best I can,

624
00:28:56.790 --> 00:29:00.783
the tools in my toolkit as tools, not as tethers.

625
00:29:02.545 --> 00:29:03.753
And I've gotten pretty,

626
00:29:06.090 --> 00:29:09.000
even more intentional about that stuff since becoming a mom.

627
00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:13.890
I also refuse to be a martyr,

628
00:29:13.890 --> 00:29:17.010
to an antiquated idea of motherhood.

629
00:29:17.010 --> 00:29:18.510
Explain that.

630
00:29:18.510 --> 00:29:22.560
That I need to be all things to all people,

631
00:29:22.560 --> 00:29:25.440
that I need to wear every hat all at once,

632
00:29:25.440 --> 00:29:29.400
I choose in any given moment what my primary identity is.

633
00:29:29.400 --> 00:29:31.560
And that's not always Athena's mom,

634
00:29:31.560 --> 00:29:33.720
it's not always Drew's wife,

635
00:29:33.720 --> 00:29:35.520
it's not always an executive at Peloton,

636
00:29:35.520 --> 00:29:37.337
it's not always an author, right?

637
00:29:37.337 --> 00:29:41.973
I'm gonna choose what piece of myself I'm utilizing

638
00:29:42.990 --> 00:29:44.515
and presenting to the world.

639
00:29:44.515 --> 00:29:46.380
And yeah, a lot of times,

640
00:29:46.380 --> 00:29:48.870
especially in the last year it's been Athena's mom

641
00:29:48.870 --> 00:29:51.150
and that's amazing, but I'm choosing when that is.

642
00:29:51.150 --> 00:29:55.110
Yeah, how does it work?

643
00:29:55.110 --> 00:29:56.970
Like speaking strictly about fitness,

644
00:29:56.970 --> 00:29:59.850
like walk me through the prenatal phase

645
00:29:59.850 --> 00:30:03.300
and how you thought about your fitness and now postnatal,

646
00:30:03.300 --> 00:30:05.370
like how you've approached it,

647
00:30:05.370 --> 00:30:08.940
whether it's different or has changed based upon

648
00:30:08.940 --> 00:30:12.163
pre mama, pre strong mama Robin.

649
00:30:12.163 --> 00:30:15.480
(laughs) Prenatal, okay, so I trained

650
00:30:15.480 --> 00:30:18.330
and I taught five days a week live

651
00:30:18.330 --> 00:30:19.880
throughout my entire pregnancy.

652
00:30:20.910 --> 00:30:21.743
It only--

653
00:30:21.743 --> 00:30:23.340
Everyone like fell in love with you 'cause you were like,

654
00:30:23.340 --> 00:30:25.170
this is like, "Oh, she's pregnant,"

655
00:30:25.170 --> 00:30:28.394
like there was a emotional bond I think that you created

656
00:30:28.394 --> 00:30:29.590
with the people that care about you.

657
00:30:29.590 --> 00:30:31.755
Well, I announced the pregnancy on the bike

658
00:30:31.755 --> 00:30:36.755
so that, it was like a very major pregnancy announcement.

659
00:30:38.070 --> 00:30:40.830
But that felt very logical to me

660
00:30:40.830 --> 00:30:44.490
'cause I have shared, parts of my life.

661
00:30:44.490 --> 00:30:47.520
Whether it's my romantic journey or my,

662
00:30:47.520 --> 00:30:50.520
of course as an athlete and as a woman, as a Latina,

663
00:30:50.520 --> 00:30:51.840
like there are aspects of myself

664
00:30:51.840 --> 00:30:56.840
that I infuse into my training and my workouts.

665
00:30:57.720 --> 00:30:59.310
And so announcing the pregnancy felt logical,

666
00:30:59.310 --> 00:31:02.040
especially 'cause I knew I was gonna teach,

667
00:31:02.040 --> 00:31:03.573
hoped to teach throughout my pregnancy

668
00:31:03.573 --> 00:31:07.530
and I had a great pregnancy, so that was possible.

669
00:31:07.530 --> 00:31:12.530
And I continued to run, strength train and cycle throughout.

670
00:31:13.800 --> 00:31:16.260
I got my prenatal certification.

671
00:31:16.260 --> 00:31:19.170
So I did prenatal classes as well for Peloton.

672
00:31:19.170 --> 00:31:24.000
And that felt, I was like, "Oh, I got this."

673
00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:28.593
Postpartum however, that piece of the journey was daunting.

674
00:31:29.520 --> 00:31:34.110
It felt like putting myself back together again,

675
00:31:34.110 --> 00:31:37.080
I just wasn't used to slowing down to that extent

676
00:31:37.080 --> 00:31:40.230
and being that vulnerable, and having no control.

677
00:31:40.230 --> 00:31:42.900
I mean just, there were so many days

678
00:31:42.900 --> 00:31:45.360
that the fatigue was crushing.

679
00:31:45.360 --> 00:31:50.360
I was recovering from a C-section so major abdominal surgery

680
00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:54.990
I mean for probably the first six weeks,

681
00:31:54.990 --> 00:31:55.823
I was like, "Oh, my God,

682
00:31:55.823 --> 00:32:00.330
am I ever gonna moved the way I'm used to moving?"

683
00:32:00.330 --> 00:32:02.400
And the pressure of being

684
00:32:02.400 --> 00:32:05.010
this celebrity fitness personality

685
00:32:05.010 --> 00:32:06.930
and what if I can't do that again

686
00:32:06.930 --> 00:32:10.205
or be that person that I want to be or know how to be?

687
00:32:10.205 --> 00:32:15.205
I had real moments of imposter syndrome,

688
00:32:17.250 --> 00:32:20.550
especially when, we are run like a network.

689
00:32:20.550 --> 00:32:23.850
So I took five months of maternity leave,

690
00:32:23.850 --> 00:32:25.920
but when we were planning for me to come back,

691
00:32:25.920 --> 00:32:28.710
they're like, production's like, "What do you wanna teach?"

692
00:32:28.710 --> 00:32:32.040
We have to put something on the live schedule for X day.

693
00:32:32.040 --> 00:32:33.780
I'm like, "I don't even physically know

694
00:32:33.780 --> 00:32:35.490
what I'm gonna be able to do."

695
00:32:35.490 --> 00:32:38.190
That felt really intense.

696
00:32:38.190 --> 00:32:43.170
And I developed a mantra then during that postpartum period

697
00:32:43.170 --> 00:32:46.020
of consistency over intensity,

698
00:32:46.020 --> 00:32:48.450
because I knew I couldn't go hard in the pain,

699
00:32:48.450 --> 00:32:49.860
which is I'm apt to do,

700
00:32:49.860 --> 00:32:54.660
like that is much more my flavor of intensity.

701
00:32:54.660 --> 00:32:56.157
And I thought just do something every day.

702
00:32:56.157 --> 00:32:58.710
And in the beginning it was literally breath work,

703
00:32:58.710 --> 00:33:00.480
like literally feeding my daughter

704
00:33:00.480 --> 00:33:02.430
and doing 360 diaphragmatic breathing.

705
00:33:02.430 --> 00:33:04.630
'Cause I knew that was gonna repair my core.

706
00:33:05.550 --> 00:33:07.830
That was weeks of that, and then it was walks

707
00:33:07.830 --> 00:33:10.200
and little by little amounting to a lot,

708
00:33:10.200 --> 00:33:12.750
but it was frustratingly slow

709
00:33:12.750 --> 00:33:17.043
and now I'm stronger than I ever have been a year later.

710
00:33:18.540 --> 00:33:21.060
And how much of that did you share transparently

711
00:33:21.060 --> 00:33:22.350
in the Peloton classes?

712
00:33:22.350 --> 00:33:25.740
Because I feel like that on some level

