00:33:25.740 --> 00:33:30.740
is much more relatable to the typical Peloton person

714
00:33:30.960 --> 00:33:33.600
than all the talk about polishing your crowns

715
00:33:33.600 --> 00:33:35.550
and all of that kind of stuff, you know what I mean?

716
00:33:35.550 --> 00:33:37.703
Like, hey, I don't feel like,

717
00:33:37.703 --> 00:33:40.560
most of the time I feel like I can barely do anything

718
00:33:40.560 --> 00:33:43.020
and now Robin can speak my language

719
00:33:43.020 --> 00:33:44.921
or I can find a relatability there

720
00:33:44.921 --> 00:33:48.720
that perhaps even strengthened your connection

721
00:33:48.720 --> 00:33:49.620
with your community.

722
00:33:49.620 --> 00:33:53.100
Definitely, I was super honest,

723
00:33:53.100 --> 00:33:55.590
especially in those first few classes back,

724
00:33:55.590 --> 00:33:57.339
in that six month period,

725
00:33:57.339 --> 00:33:59.820
my first six months back on the bike

726
00:33:59.820 --> 00:34:01.353
and back in strength classes,

727
00:34:02.490 --> 00:34:04.590
I'd already been doing my own training

728
00:34:04.590 --> 00:34:06.870
during my maternity leave, but it's different.

729
00:34:06.870 --> 00:34:09.060
It's different during, in front of the camera that first,

730
00:34:09.060 --> 00:34:11.850
those first few sprints (laughs) feel like,

731
00:34:11.850 --> 00:34:14.640
am I ever gonna get it back, but your body does remember.

732
00:34:14.640 --> 00:34:16.890
And I think being honest about that journey,

733
00:34:16.890 --> 00:34:21.890
especially as a woman and very anti-snap back culture.

734
00:34:22.560 --> 00:34:23.400
I wanna talk about that

735
00:34:23.400 --> 00:34:24.600
because there is all this pressure,

736
00:34:24.600 --> 00:34:28.110
like how quickly can you get back to where you were before?

737
00:34:28.110 --> 00:34:31.680
And your whole thing is about letting go of what was before

738
00:34:31.680 --> 00:34:33.390
and let's focus on moving forward.

739
00:34:33.390 --> 00:34:35.343
Yeah, And I really,

740
00:34:37.320 --> 00:34:40.350
my refrain was what if a plateau is a launching pad?

741
00:34:40.350 --> 00:34:42.450
What if a plateau is a launching pad?

742
00:34:42.450 --> 00:34:44.583
And for a really long time,

743
00:34:46.783 --> 00:34:48.183
I still wasn't fitting into,

744
00:34:49.350 --> 00:34:52.020
like I'm supposed to wear the new Peloton collection

745
00:34:52.020 --> 00:34:53.610
and I'd have to go back and be like,

746
00:34:53.610 --> 00:34:56.820
I actually still need this other size, you know?

747
00:34:56.820 --> 00:35:00.480
And I had to tell my reframe the story around that

748
00:35:00.480 --> 00:35:02.520
and focus on what my body could do

749
00:35:02.520 --> 00:35:06.540
rather than what size the tag said.

750
00:35:06.540 --> 00:35:09.900
Sure, and it's all good now though, feel strong?

751
00:35:09.900 --> 00:35:11.283
I'm stronger than ever.

752
00:35:12.510 --> 00:35:14.340
But it was little by little amounting to a lot.

753
00:35:14.340 --> 00:35:18.840
I mean, it was truly like the smallest steps.

754
00:35:18.840 --> 00:35:21.063
I remember runs on the west-side highway.

755
00:35:23.076 --> 00:35:26.393
I trained for the, I ran the New York City Marathon about,

756
00:35:28.260 --> 00:35:29.790
I think Athena was nine months.

757
00:35:29.790 --> 00:35:33.330
And I didn't, when I tell you that I didn't look at a watch.

758
00:35:33.330 --> 00:35:37.470
I would old school like map the distance for my runs

759
00:35:37.470 --> 00:35:41.340
and not run with a single stitch of like pacing,

760
00:35:41.340 --> 00:35:45.420
because I couldn't even take that information,

761
00:35:45.420 --> 00:35:47.700
I couldn't be like, "Oh, but your pace was this and da da,"

762
00:35:47.700 --> 00:35:50.580
no way, I showed up to the New York City Marathon

763
00:35:50.580 --> 00:35:52.440
actually having zero idea how long it was gonna take me.

764
00:35:52.440 --> 00:35:53.430
Like I was just like--

765
00:35:53.430 --> 00:35:54.347
It's liberating that way.

766
00:35:54.347 --> 00:35:56.879
It was so liberating and it was a nice,

767
00:35:56.879 --> 00:36:01.350
it was a refreshing back to basics.

768
00:36:01.350 --> 00:36:03.530
Like it was like, I'm doing this because I love it,

769
00:36:03.530 --> 00:36:07.110
and because I feel better doing it

770
00:36:07.110 --> 00:36:10.170
rather than any external gaze.

771
00:36:10.170 --> 00:36:11.370
Yeah, I shared a little thing

772
00:36:11.370 --> 00:36:14.040
about this on Instagram the other day.

773
00:36:14.040 --> 00:36:15.960
My version of that is just getting older

774
00:36:15.960 --> 00:36:17.640
and dealing with injuries,

775
00:36:17.640 --> 00:36:20.610
it's a limited version of what you experienced

776
00:36:20.610 --> 00:36:21.720
on an extreme level,

777
00:36:21.720 --> 00:36:26.130
but at some point the GPS watches and all the stuff

778
00:36:26.130 --> 00:36:29.634
are no longer tools, but they're vehicles to shame yourself.

779
00:36:29.634 --> 00:36:32.610
